From: Armada Houji maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: omit Houji placeholder power

Houji's firmware reports a constant 10000000 for the translated POWER_NOW
property, independent of the changing gauge voltage/current. Advertising it
causes consumers such as btop to prefer a fictitious 10 W reading. It also
selects their energy-based time estimator although this gauge exports charge.

Do not advertise this unsupported measurement on Houji. Keep the measured
VOLTAGE_NOW and CURRENT_NOW so consumers can derive watts and use the gauge's
charge counter. Leave the property on Qualcomm variants that implement it.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1192,7 +1192,8 @@ static const enum power_supply_property houji_bat_props[] = {
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TIME_TO_EMPTY_AVG,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_INTERNAL_RESISTANCE,
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATE_OF_HEALTH,
-	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_POWER_NOW,
+	/* Firmware's POWER_NOW is a fixed placeholder, not gauge telemetry.
+	 * Consumers can use CURRENT_NOW and VOLTAGE_NOW instead. */
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CONSTANT_CHARGE_CURRENT,
 };
 
